00:23:03.320 --> 00:23:08.880
So first of all, my recommendation
never let AI create the project.

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.200
First of all,
you just waste tokens if you do that.

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:16.640
But if you do that, you probably end up
with an outdated application.

00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:21.240
So if you have like spring, for example,
in the trial field, there's Spring Initializr

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:22.760
that you can create an application,

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:25.880
you get the newest dependencies,
you get in the way.

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:29.520
How the spring team currently
thinks about creating applications.

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:31.640
Maybe you have a CLI for your tools.

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:32.320
Use that.

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:33.880
Don't use AI for that.

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:36.040
And then you have to define the rules.

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:41.280
So that means you don't put everything
in Claude.md or in the AGENTS.md

00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:44.800
because there's a study
